# --- Speedrun held-out data (T-01) — see speedrun/eval/holdout/MANIFEST.md ---
# The anki-revlogs-10k corpus is licensed for individual research use and its
# licence forbids public redistribution. No part of it may enter this public
# fork, in any form, and the leakage check has to be able to demonstrate that.
speedrun/**/anki-revlogs-10k/
speedrun/eval/corpus/
speedrun/eval/.hf_cache/
# h1_reviews.jsonl is a derivative of that corpus (real reviews), so the same
# licence applies. Its SHA-256 is recorded in MANIFEST.md; the data stays local.
speedrun/eval/holdout/h1_reviews.jsonl
speedrun/eval/holdout/raw/
# Raw review data and collection files never commit: review history is the
# student's own study data, and Speedrun treats the collection as a sensor it
# reads and never republishes. Only hashes and derived numbers commit.
speedrun/eval/holdout/*.parquet
speedrun/eval/holdout/*.anki2
speedrun/eval/holdout/*.colpkg
# The student's deck is the sensor, not our content. We read it and never
# republish it (ADR-0005), so no deck file enters this fork in any format —
# quite apart from the 238 MB one being larger than GitHub accepts. Only the
# derived label inventory and the granularity report commit.
# Add-on runtime state. meta.json is generated at install and rewritten by Anki
# whenever the add-on is toggled or reconfigured, so it is a local artifact and
# never the shipped configuration.
speedrun/addon/meta.json
speedrun/addon/user_files/
speedrun/eval/deck/*.apkg
speedrun/eval/deck/*.colpkg
speedrun/eval/deck/*.anki2
speedrun/eval/deck/media*
